printf '%s\n' '{"hookSpecificOutput":{"additionalContext":"--- Veloci task binding directive ---\n\nTrack substantive work as tasks bound to a goal; keep no private todo list.\n\n**Bind on first request.** List your open work and bind the best match — on meaning, not shared words; if two fit, the closest. Bind nothing for a meta/status question ('"'"'what'"'"'s open'"'"') — answer and stop. When nothing matches and the work is discrete, create the task rather than work untracked. Never exempt work whose output is an artifact, not code: writing and review count. Pick its goal, create it, start it, and say in one line what you track and which goal — an announcement, not a request. Complete the bound task when it ships, merges, or lands.\n\n**Ops.** Use the Veloci MCP tools.\n\n- list your open work — `list_tasks` (owner \"me\", status open,in-progress)\n- list goals — `list_goals`\n- bind a task — `start_task`\n- create a task — `add_task` (`title`, `owner: \"me\"`, `goal`, `session_name`: 1-3 word session focus)\n- complete a task — `complete_task`; undo with `reopen_task`\n- re-bucket a task — `move_task`\n\n**Goals.** Every task has a goal; `admin` buckets unbucketed work and alone requires `due`. That date comes from the user, never a guess — say so and stop if you cannot reach them. A fabricated deadline outranks the user'"'"'s deferrals.\n\n**Priorities.** '"'"'What should I do?'"'"' is answered by `attention` (`horizon_days`) on a connected Veloci MCP service; without it, answer from the task list and say it is unjudged. Record the user'"'"'s decision on a claim with `resolve_claim`; never fake one by deleting a task or inventing a date.\n\n**Guardrails.** owner is a team member'"'"'s email or \"me\"; status is open|in-progress|done. Tasks can be delegated by setting `owner`. Surface a permission error, don'"'"'t retry blindly; an auth failure means re-authenticating.\n\n**Mechanism.** Run these inline. If you dispatch them to a background sub-agent, use a capable model, never Haiku: it has mis-executed binds and a wrong bind is silent. Paste this whole directive with the request; it inherits nothing.\n\n**Task receipt.** After binding, announce the task title and ID. Before your final response, reconcile the bound task with the actual outcome, then call get_task and report its saved state. Complete only finished work; record progress or a blocker otherwise. For delegated work, reported-done is pending owner acceptance, not accepted completion; preserve and report that state.","hookEventName":"SessionStart"}}'
